\DOC ABBREV_TRACE_TAC

\TYPE {ABBREV_TRACE_TAC : thm list ref -> tactic}

\SYNOPSIS
Replaces the assumption describing a state's current event trace by one stating
that the trace equals a freshly abbreviated trace term applied to the goal's
parameters, swaps in the corresponding bounds assumption for the new
abbreviation, and leaves the conclusion unchanged.

\DESCRIBE
The single argument {stored_abbrevs : thm list ref} is a mutable reference cell
in which the tactic records the abbreviation theorems it creates; it is not
part of the goal and nothing of it appears in the resulting goals. Applied to
{A ?- t}, the tactic locates in {A} the assumption equating a state's event
list {u} with an explicit prefix of concrete event constructors applied to an
older abbreviated trace (or to the trailing trace variable), removes it, and
adds instead an assumption equating {u} with a new trace constant applied to
the goal's address/pc/stackpointer parameters. The bounds assumption for the
old trace abbreviation is likewise removed, and the analogous bounds assumption
for the new abbreviation is added at the end of the assumption list, so the
remaining assumptions are merely renumbered.
{
       A, u = oldprefix, bounds oldtrace ?- t
       ====================================== ABBREV_TRACE_TAC stored_abbrevs
       A, u = newtrace..., bounds newtrace ?- t
}

\COMMENTS
The observed traces show only this single-subgoal rewriting of trace
assumptions in machine-state goals about eventual execution, always with such a
pair of trace assumptions present.

\ENDDOC
